# GenSeo ticket queue

`daily-tickets.md` is consumed top to bottom: the runner takes the FIRST heading that still contains `[ ]`, and
the wrapper counts open tickets with `grep -cE '^(- \[ \]|## \[ \])'`. Zero open = the day stops.

## Editing rules
- Append only, as a new `# BATCH <YYYY-MM-DD> (...)` section at the end. Never reorder, rewrite or delete
  `[DONE …]`, `[x]`, `[SKIPPED-…]` tickets — they are the dedup history.
- Ticket ids never collide across hosts: Mac Mini `#NN`, MacBook `#MBmmdd-N`, refill on the Mini `#MMmmdd-N`,
  Cursor Cloud `#CAmmdd-N`.
- After any edit: `python3 scripts/lint_tickets.py daily-tickets.md` must exit 0 (it fails on a banned AgeAura link
  or a Urolithin mention inside an open ticket).

## Ticket format (what `refill_tickets.py` renders)
```
- [ ] **#CA1009-1 — <primary keyword>** — `<Title, ≤60 chars, (US 2026)>`
  - **Primary keyword:** `<primary>` · **Secondary:** a, b, c
  - **Search intent:** <who is searching and what they will decide>
  - **Template:** EDITORIAL|STORY|LISTICLE|COMPARISON · **Gate:** topic_fitness <verdict> · suggest.json <result>
  - **Hero product:** `/products/<handle>` (<name>, $<live price>, live <date>)
  - **Collection links (≥2, verify live):** `/collections/<a>`, `/collections/<b>` (+ membership notes)
  - **Angle:** <the one thing this article answers that no live article does>
  - **Fan-out answers to cover:** <follow-up questions, each a self-contained 40–80-word answer>
  - **Evidence to fetch & confirm (claims log):** <studies/labels to fetch — never cite unfetched>
  - **Link, don't restate:** `/blogs/news/<live handle>`, …
  - **Author:** roster.json byline — exact name + bio at write time; never invent a person or credential
  - **Dedup note:** <family + segment checked against N live articles and every ticket in the file>
```

## Refill (no Ads/GSC needed)
- `python3 scripts/refill_tickets.py --count 8 --dry-run` prints the batch and every rejected candidate with its
  reason; drop `--dry-run` to append (lint is re-run and the append is rolled back if it fails).
- Sources, in order: `board/ideas.csv` rows with `status=idea`, then `templates/article-topic-bank.json`. The
  script never invents topics — to add runway, add a vetted bank topic or a board idea, then dry-run.
- Gates every candidate must pass: brand_rules → hero live + in stock → not a covered topic from the queue header
  (rule 6) → not already queued (any status) → not already live (family + segment, Jaccard ≥ 0.72, handle) →
  `topic_fitness.assess()` strict on primary AND title under every stocked-brand token = PASS or
  REVIEW [covered-segment] → live `suggest.json` returns 0 articles for the primary.
- One article per brand + segment pair, ever. `topic_fitness` only recognises its `SEGMENT_MODIFIERS`
  (for beginners, for athletes, over 60, dosage, how long, morning or night, where to buy, price, …); a primary
  without one FAILs `[covered]` once the brand has any article. Do not edit `topic_fitness.py` to widen this —
  that is Kevin's call.
- Board columns: `id,status,product,primary_keyword,working_title,segment,intent,template,angle,volume,source,
  ticket_id,added,updated`. `status`: idea → queued → done/skipped (synced from the queue). `volume` = real data
  only, otherwise `No data`.
